<title>MEXICO: Mexico Jan-Aug oil exports average 1.531 mln bpd.</title>
<headline>Mexico Jan-Aug oil exports average 1.531 mln bpd.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican oil exports in the January to August period averaged 1.531 million barrels per day, earning $6.603 billion, up $1.489 billion from the same period in 1995, Petroleos Mexicanos (Pemex) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The state oil company said Isthmus sales abroad averaged 186,700 bpd, bringing in revenues of $854 million. Heavy Maya crude exports in the eight-month period were 861,900 bpd, worth $3.383 billion.</p>
<p>Mexico sold 482,400 bpd of extra-light Olmeca crude, worth $2.366 billion. The average price per barrel of Isthmus was $18.75, Maya was $16.09 and Olmeca, $20.10, Pemex said.</p>
<p>-- Henry Tricks, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9560</p>
